	(text_box "Main Functions:\n\nAutomatic Power Switching: The circuit allows your device to run from either VCC (main power supply) OR the battery (CR1220), whichever has the higher voltage.\nBattery Backup: When VCC is present and higher than the battery voltage, the system runs on VCC. When VCC drops or fails, the battery automatically takes over without interruption.\nPrevents Back-feeding: The two Schottky diodes (BAT54C) prevent current from flowing backward:\n\nVCC cannot charge or drain the battery\nThe battery cannot feed back into the VCC line\n\n\n\nHow It Works:\n\nNormal operation: VCC is present → top diode conducts → powers the circuit → bottom diode blocks (preventing battery drain)\nPower failure: VCC drops → top diode blocks → bottom diode conducts → battery powers the circuit\nC1 (0.1µF): Provides local decoupling/filtering for stable voltage\n\nTypical Applications:\n\nReal-time clock (RTC) circuits\nMemory retention (SRAM, configuration data)\nMicrocontroller backup power\nAny low-power circuit requiring uninterrupted operation during power loss"
