	(text_box "PCB Layout Tips:\n\nTrace lengths: Keep SDMMC traces short (<75mm) and equal length\nTrace width: Use 0.2-0.3mm (8-12 mil) traces for signal lines\nGround plane: Use solid ground plane under socket\nSpacing: Keep clock trace away from data/command lines\nDecoupling: Place 0.1µF cap as close as possible to VDD pin\n\n\nSoftware Configuration (STM32CubeMX):\n\nEnable SDMMC1 peripheral\nSet PC8-PC12, PD2 as SDMMC1 alternate functions\nSet PA8 (or your chosen pin) as GPIO Input with pull-up\nConfigure SDMMC1 clock to 50 MHz max\nUse 4-bit wide bus mode for best performance\n\n\nTesting Steps:\n\nPower check: Verify 3.3V on pin 4, GND on pins 6,9\nPull-ups: Check ~3.3V on all data/CMD lines when no card inserted\nCard detect: Should read LOW when card inserted\nClock signal: Should toggle when SDMMC initialized\nFatFs test: Try to mount card and read/write files"
